    "DKA usually occurs as a consequence of absolute or relative insulin deficiency that is accompanied by an increase in counter regulatory hormones (i.e., glucagon, cortisol, growth hormone, catecholamines).",
    "In the majority of cases people with type 1 diabetes should be under specialist care.",
