    "Where an individual with type 1 diabetes is using an insulin pump or closed loop system, dir",
    "For individuals using insulin pump/closed loop systems, follow the latest JBDS-IP guidelines on using technology to support diabetes care in hospital(12):",
    "If using insulin pump/hybrid closed loop system, seek specialist diabetes advice for an individualised care plan.",
    "You can use a needle and syringe, an insulin pen, or an insulin pump.", "Some people use a CGM as part of an artificial pancreas. An artificial pancreas is a system that mimics how a healthy pancreas controls blood glucose in the body. A CGM, an insulin pump, and a software program that shares information between the CGM and insulin pump make up the artificial pancreas.",
    "For some people, especially those using insulin pumps and/or wearable glucose sensors, a range of 4-6mmol/L may be their normal when they are not eating.",
    "For those on insulin pumps, review of their use of the device and provision of further education in the use of such technology, as necessary",
    "In those using an insulin pump, if transfer to a Level 2 / HDU or ITU is necessary, then the pump should be stopped, removed and stored safely." .

