<https://example.org/dmo/id/drugClass/sulfonylurea> <https://example.org/dmo#evidenceQuote>
    "It is also important to check for the occurrence of and frequency of hypoglycaemia when conducting reviews in the postoperative phase for all individuals with diabetes on sulfonylurea, meglitinides or insulin therapies.",
    "Hypoglycaemia is the commonest side-effect of insulin or sulfonylurea therapy used to treat diabetes.",
    "for people receiving insulin or sulfonylurea therapy as treatment for their diabetes, evidence would suggest that achieving good glycaemic control while avoiding hypoglycaemia remains very difficult.",
    "If the hypoglycaemia was caused by sulfonylurea or long-acting insulin therapy then be aware the risk of hypoglycaemia may persist for up to 24-36 hours following the last dose, especially if there is concurrent renal impairment.",
    "Promote the prescription of hypoglycaemia “rescue” treatment for all people with diabetes in hospital on insulin or sulfonylurea therapy." .

