<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/include-nutrient-rich-foods-in-meal-plan>
  <https://example.org/dmo#evidenceQuote> "Try to choose foods that include nutrients such as vitamins, calcium, fiber, and healthy fats." .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/learn-healthy-ways-to-lower-stress-and-seek-help-from-health-care-team-or-mental-health-professional>
  <https://example.org/dmo#evidenceQuote> "Learn healthy ways to lower your stress NIH external link, and ask for help from your health care team or a mental health professional." .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/learn-how-to-treat-low-blood-glucose-and-inform-others>
  <https://example.org/dmo#evidenceQuote> "You can learn how to treat low blood glucose, let other people know what to do if you need help, and use a medical alert bracelet." .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/lose-5-to-7-of-current-weight-to-improve-health-outcomes>
  <https://example.org/dmo#evidenceQuote> "Losing 5% to 7% of your current weight may help you prevent or improve some health problems and manage your blood glucose, cholesterol, and blood pressure levels." .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/plan-healthy-meals-and-snacks> <https://example.org/dmo#evidenceQuote>
    "To have a healthy lifestyle, take steps now to plan healthy meals and snacks, do physical activities, get enough sleep, and quit smoking or using tobacco products." .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/plate-method-composition> <https://example.org/dmo#evidenceQuote>
    "Nonstarchy vegetables—such as leafy greens, peppers, carrots, or green beans—should make up half of your plate. Carb foods that are high in fiber—such as brown rice, whole grains, beans, or fruits—should make up one-quarter of your plate. Protein foods—such as lean meats, fish, dairy, or tofu or other soy products—should make up one quarter of your plate." .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/strength-training-twice-weekly> <https://example.org/dmo#evidenceQuote>
    "Try to do this kind of training two times a week." .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/take-care-of-feet-before-during-and-after-physical-activity>
  <https://example.org/dmo#evidenceQuote> "Take care of your feet before, during, and after physical activity." .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/take-steps-to-protect-yourself-from-low-blood-glucose>
  <https://example.org/dmo#evidenceQuote> "Low blood glucose can be a serious medical emergency that must be treated right away. Take steps to protect yourself." .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/talk-with-health-care-professional-about-mental-health-if-experiencing-stress-sadness-or-anger>
  <https://example.org/dmo#evidenceQuote> "Having diabetes can be stressful. Talk with your health care professional or health care team if you need help." .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/talk-with-health-care-professional-about-weight-loss-programs-with-support-and-counseling>
  <https://example.org/dmo#evidenceQuote> "You may want to talk with your health care professional about other options for managing your weight, including joining a weight-loss program that can provide helpful information, support, and behavioral or lifestyle counseling." .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/talk-with-health-care-professional-before-starting-new-physical-activity>
  <https://example.org/dmo#evidenceQuote> "Talk with your health care professional before starting a new physical activity or changing how much physical activity you do." .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/talk-with-health-care-professional-before-starting-weight-loss-plan-for-child-with-diabetes>
  <https://example.org/dmo#evidenceQuote> "If you are worried about your child’s weight and they have diabetes, talk with their health care professional before your child starts a new weight-loss plan." .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/talk-with-health-care-professional-before-taking-dietary-supplements>
  <https://example.org/dmo#evidenceQuote> "Talk with your health care professional before you take any supplements, because some may cause side effects or affect how well your diabetes medicines work." .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/use-carb-counting-or-plate-method-for-portion-control>
  <https://example.org/dmo#evidenceQuote> "For people who have diabetes, carb counting and the plate method are two common ways to plan how much to eat or drink. Talk with your health care professional or health care team to find a method that works for you." .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/use-carb-counting-to-adjust-insulin-dose>
  <https://example.org/dmo#evidenceQuote> "Not all people with diabetes need to count carbs. However, if you take insulin, counting carbs can help you know how much insulin to take." .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/use-online-tools-like-body-weight-planner-to-create-eating-and-physical-activity-plans>
  <https://example.org/dmo#evidenceQuote> "Online tools such as the Body Weight Planner may help you create eating and physical activity plans." .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/work-with-health-care-team-to-create-a-weight-loss-plan-if-overweight-or-obese>
  <https://example.org/dmo#evidenceQuote> "If you are an adult with overweight or obesity, work with your health care team to create a weight-loss plan." .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/work-with-health-care-team-to-create-personalized-meal-plan>
  <https://example.org/dmo#evidenceQuote> "Work with your health care team to create a meal plan that works for you." .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/riskFactor/diabetes-mellitus> <https://example.org/dmo#evidenceQuote>
    "If you have diabetes, managing your weight may bring you several health benefits." .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/riskFactor/type-1-diabetes> <https://example.org/dmo#evidenceQuote>
    "DKA is most common in people with type 1 diabetes. Occasionally, DKA may affect people with type 2 diabetes who have lost their ability to produce insulin." .

