    "Allowing people to easily identify the amount of carbohydrate consumed (by providing easily identified 10g “bricks” of carbohydrate) can allow them to carbohydrate count." .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/lifestyleIntervention/diabetes-training-for-non-specialist-medical-staff>
  <https://example.org/dmo#evidenceQuote> "Using a variety of measures including proactive identification of admissions involving people with diabetes, online referral system, use of web-linked glucose meters, an enhanced diabetes team and diabetes training for non-specialist medical staff, a hospital in England was able to demonstrate a reduced length of stay over and above improvements seen across all hospital patients (41)." .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/lifestyleIntervention/hypoglycaemia-education> <https://example.org/dmo#evidenceQuote>
