<https://example.org/dmo/id/symptom/acidosis> <https://example.org/dmo#evidenceQuote>
    "Diabetic ketoacidosis (DKA) is a complex disordered metabolic state characterised by hyperglycaemia, ketonaemia, and acidosis." .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/symptom/acute-myocardial-infarction> <https://example.org/dmo#evidenceQuote>
    "The main causes of mortality in the adult population include severe hypokalaemia, adult respiratory distress syndrome, and co-morbid states which may have precipitated the DKA such as pneumonia, acute myocardial infarction and sepsis (25)." .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/symptom/adult-respiratory-distress-syndrome> <https://example.org/dmo#evidenceQuote>
    "The main causes of mortality in the adult population include severe hypokalaemia, adult respiratory distress syndrome, and co-morbid states which may have precipitated the DKA such as pneumonia, acute myocardial infarction and sepsis (25)." .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/symptom/blurred-eyesight> <https://example.org/dmo#evidenceQuote>
    "Later signs/symptoms include dehydration (manifesting as dry skin and mouth), blurred eyesight, tachypnoea, rapid pulse, a distinct smell on the breath (sometimes described as ‘pear drops’) and coma." .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/symptom/cerebral-oedema> <https://example.org/dmo#evidenceQuote>
    "Cerebral oedema remains the most common cause of mortality, particularly in young children and adolescents." .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/symptom/dehydration> <https://example.org/dmo#evidenceQuote>
    "Later signs/symptoms include dehydration (manifesting as dry skin and mouth), blurred eyesight, tachypnoea, rapid pulse, a distinct smell on the breath (sometimes described as ‘pear drops’) and coma." .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/symptom/diminished-level-of-consciousness> <https://example.org/dmo#evidenceQuote>
    "There are several mechanisms responsible for fluid depletion in DKA. These include osmotic diuresis due to hyperglycaemia, vomiting - commonly associated with DKA - and eventually, inability to take in fluid due to a diminished level of consciousness." .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/symptom/distinct-smell-on-the-breath> <https://example.org/dmo#evidenceQuote>
    "Later signs/symptoms include dehydration (manifesting as dry skin and mouth), blurred eyesight, tachypnoea, rapid pulse, a distinct smell on the breath (sometimes described as ‘pear drops’) and coma." .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/symptom/drowsy-individual> <https://example.org/dmo#evidenceQuote>
    "a drowsy individual in the context of DKA is seriously concerning and the person requires critical care assessment." .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/symptom/hyperkalaemia> <https://example.org/dmo#evidenceQuote>
    "Electrolyte shifts and depletion are in part related to the osmotic diuresis. Hyperkalaemia and hypokalaemia need particular attention." .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/symptom/hypotension> <https://example.org/dmo#evidenceQuote>
    "Systolic BP (SBP) on admission below 90 mmHg" .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/symptom/ketonaemia> <https://example.org/dmo#evidenceQuote>
    "Diabetic ketoacidosis (DKA) is a complex disordered metabolic state characterised by hyperglycaemia, ketonaemia, and acidosis." .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/symptom/leg-cramps> <https://example.org/dmo#evidenceQuote>
    "Symptoms include nausea and/or vomiting, abdominal pain, polyuria and polydipsia, and leg cramps." .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/symptom/nausea-and-or-vomiting> <https://example.org/dmo#evidenceQuote>
    "Symptoms include nausea and/or vomiting, abdominal pain, polyuria and polydipsia, and leg cramps." .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/symptom/osmotic-diuresis-due-to-hyperglycaemia> <https://example.org/dmo#evidenceQuote>
    "There are several mechanisms responsible for fluid depletion in DKA. These include osmotic diuresis due to hyperglycaemia, vomiting - commonly associated with DKA - and eventually, inability to take in fluid due to a diminished level of consciousness." .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/symptom/pneumonia> <https://example.org/dmo#evidenceQuote>
    "The main causes of mortality in the adult population include severe hypokalaemia, adult respiratory distress syndrome, and co-morbid states which may have precipitated the DKA such as pneumonia, acute myocardial infarction and sepsis (25)." .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/symptom/polydipsia> <https://example.org/dmo#evidenceQuote>
    "Symptoms include nausea and/or vomiting, abdominal pain, polyuria and polydipsia, and leg cramps." .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/symptom/rapid-pulse> <https://example.org/dmo#evidenceQuote>
    "Later signs/symptoms include dehydration (manifesting as dry skin and mouth), blurred eyesight, tachypnoea, rapid pulse, a distinct smell on the breath (sometimes described as ‘pear drops’) and coma." .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/symptom/sepsis> <https://example.org/dmo#evidenceQuote>
    "The main causes of mortality in the adult population include severe hypokalaemia, adult respiratory distress syndrome, and co-morbid states which may have precipitated the DKA such as pneumonia, acute myocardial infarction and sepsis (25)." .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/symptom/severe-hypokalaemia> <https://example.org/dmo#evidenceQuote>
    "The main causes of mortality in the adult population include severe hypokalaemia, adult respiratory distress syndrome, and co-morbid states which may have precipitated the DKA such as pneumonia, acute myocardial infarction and sepsis (25)." .

