<https://example.org/dmo/id/lifestyleIntervention/limit-the-amount-of-fat-in-your-eating-plan-eat-more-plant-based-foods-and-get-regular-physical-activity>
  <https://example.org/dmo#activityTarget> "limit the amount of fat in your eating plan, eat more plant-based foods, and get regular physical activity" .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/lifestyleIntervention/stop-smoking> <https://example.org/dmo#activityTarget>
    "stop smoking", "Stop smoking." .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/lifestyleIntervention/be-more-physically-active> <https://example.org/dmo#activityTarget>
    "Choose activities that are easy on your feet, such as walking, dancing, yoga or stretching, swimming, or bike riding." .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/lifestyleIntervention/trim-your-toenails-straight-across>
  <https://example.org/dmo#activityTarget> "Using toenail clippers, trim your toenails straight across. Do not cut into the corners of your toenail. Gently smooth each nail with an emery board or nonsharp nail file." .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/lifestyleIntervention/wear-shoes-and-socks-at-all-times>
  <https://example.org/dmo#activityTarget> "Wear shoes and socks at all times. Do not walk barefoot or in just socks – even when you are indoors." .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/lifestyleIntervention/aerobic-activities> <https://example.org/dmo#activityTarget>
    "Walk, dance, wheelchair roll, or swim for at least 150 minutes of moderate-intensity activity per week, or 30 minutes a day on most days of the week" .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/lifestyleIntervention/balance-and-stretching-activities>
  <https://example.org/dmo#activityTarget> "Stand on one leg or stretch legs while sitting on the floor, two or three times a week" .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/lifestyleIntervention/healthy-meal-plan> <https://example.org/dmo#activityTarget>
    "Include dairy or plant-based dairy products, fruits, nonstarchy vegetables, protein foods, and whole grains; choose foods with vitamins, calcium, fiber, and healthy fats; limit foods high in saturated fat, sodium, and added sugar; limit alcohol; consider carb counting or the plate method for portion control" .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/lifestyleIntervention/physical-activity> <https://example.org/dmo#activityTarget>
    "Check your blood glucose level before, during, and right after physical activity",
    "adjust your level of activity based on how active you were before your pregnancy" .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/lifestyleIntervention/plate-method> <https://example.org/dmo#activityTarget>
    "Divide a 9-inch plate into three sections: half nonstarchy vegetables, one-quarter high-fiber carb foods, and one-quarter protein foods" .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/lifestyleIntervention/quit-smoking-or-using-tobacco-products>
  <https://example.org/dmo#activityTarget> "Quit smoking or using tobacco products" .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/lifestyleIntervention/reach-or-maintain-a-healthy-weight>
  <https://example.org/dmo#activityTarget> "Reach and maintain a healthy weight through a healthy meal plan, regular physical activity, and other healthy behaviors" .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/lifestyleIntervention/strength-training-or-resistance-training>
  <https://example.org/dmo#activityTarget> "Lift weights or do exercises such as wall pushups or arm raises, two times a week" .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/lifestyleIntervention/weight-management> <https://example.org/dmo#activityTarget>
    "Losing 5% to 7% of your current weight" .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/lifestyleIntervention/brisk-walking-for-150-minutes-each-week>
  <https://example.org/dmo#activityTarget> "150 minutes of moderate-intensity physical activity per week" .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/lifestyleIntervention/weight-loss-surgery> <https://example.org/dmo#activityTarget>
    "help some people who have obesity and type 2 diabetes lose a large amount of weight and bring their blood glucose levels back to a healthy range" .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/lifestyleIntervention/reach-and-maintain-a-healthy-weight>
  <https://example.org/dmo#activityTarget> "To lose weight, you may need to consume fewer calories or get more physical activity." .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/lifestyleIntervention/avoid-alcoholic-beverages> <https://example.org/dmo#activityTarget>
    "avoid drinking alcoholic beverages throughout pregnancy" .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/lifestyleIntervention/breastfeeding> <https://example.org/dmo#activityTarget>
    "Helping you to lose weight after delivery" .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/lifestyleIntervention/medical-nutrition-therapy> <https://example.org/dmo#activityTarget>
    "counseling to help you create and follow a meal plan" .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/lifestyleIntervention/regular-physical-activity> <https://example.org/dmo#activityTarget>
    "at least 150 minutes of moderate-intensity physical activity, such as brisk walking, each week" .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/lifestyleIntervention/regular-physical-activity-and-lost-5-to-7-of-their-body-weight>
  <https://example.org/dmo#activityTarget> "Regular physical activity and lost 5% to 7% of their body weight" .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/lifestyleIntervention/carbohydrate-counting> <https://example.org/dmo#activityTarget>
    "Providing easily identified 10g \"bricks\" of carbohydrate to allow people to easily identify the amount of carbohydrate consumed" .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/lifestyleIntervention/diabetes-training-for-non-specialist-medical-staff>
  <https://example.org/dmo#activityTarget> "Training non-specialist medical staff in diabetes care" .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/lifestyleIntervention/self-management-of-hypoglycaemia>
  <https://example.org/dmo#activityTarget> "People capable of self-care should alert nursing staff an episode of hypoglycaemia has occurred so their management plan can be altered if necessary" .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/lifestyleIntervention/support-for-self-management-when-capable-and-appropriate>
  <https://example.org/dmo#activityTarget> "Many people with diabetes carry their own supplies of oral carbohydrate and should be supported to self-manage when capable and appropriate" .

