    "Test to assess kidney function" .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/KidneyFailure> <https://example.org/dmo#definition> "Kidney failure means that your kidneys have lost most of their ability to function—less than 15 percent of normal kidney function." .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/CKD> <https://example.org/dmo#definition> "The two key markers for chronic kidney disease (CKD) are urine albumin and estimated glomerular filtration rate (eGFR)." .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/complication/macroalbuminuria> <https://example.org/dmo#definition>
    "Macroalbuminuria is sometimes used to describe albumin levels more than 300mg/g." .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/complication/microalbuminuria> <https://example.org/dmo#definition>
    "Microalbuminuria is a term used to describe urine albumin levels not detected by a dipstick test, i.e., 30 mg/g–300 mg/g." .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/labTest/egfr> <https://example.org/dmo#definition> "Estimated glomerular filtration rate, a measure of kidney function." .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/labTest/uacr> <https://example.org/dmo#definition> "A measure of albumin excretion in urine, used to assess kidney damage in diabetes." .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/HeartFailure> <https://example.org/dmo#definition> "TZD 类药物的告知项。原文：Before you start taking these drugs, tell your doctor if you have heart failure." .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/LiverDisease> <https://example.org/dmo#definition> "多个药物类别的共同告知项。原文反复出现 tell your doctor if you have heart, liver, or kidney problems。" .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/complication/acute-kidney-injury> <https://example.org/dmo#definition>
    "Acute kidney injury (AKI) contributes to reduced metformin clearance." .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/complication/albuminuria> <https://example.org/dmo#definition>
    "Albuminuria is defined as ACR $30 mg/g" .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/complication/atherosclerotic-cardiovascular-disease> <https://example.org/dmo#definition>
    "Atherosclerotic cardiovascular disease (ASCVD) refers to the buildup of plaque in the arteries, leading to conditions such as coronary artery disease, cerebrovascular disease, and peripheral artery disease." .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/complication/cardiovascular-disease> <https://example.org/dmo#definition>
    "CVD refers to conditions such as coronary heart disease, ischemic stroke, and other cardiovascular events, which are more common in patients with diabetes and CKD.",
    "大血管病变主要是指动脉粥样硬化性心血管疾病和心力衰竭，其中动脉粥样硬化性心血管疾病包括冠心病、脑血管疾病和周围血管疾病。", "advanced diabetes complications such as chronic kidney disease, nerve problems, or cardiovascular disease" .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/complication/diabetic-ketoacidosis> <https://example.org/dmo#definition>
    "Diabetic ketoacidosis (DKA) is a serious complication of diabetes characterized by hyperglycemia, ketonemia, and metabolic acidosis, often requiring emergency treatment.",
    "DKA is a serious complication of diabetes that can be life-threatening. DKA is most common among people with type 1 diabetes. People with type 2 diabetes can also develop DKA.",
    "Risk of DKA if insulin is stopped or dose is inadequate, particularly in insulin-treated individuals.",
    "因急性高血糖引起的糖尿病酮症酸中毒、高渗性高血糖状态等急性并发症，如救治不及时可能危及生命。", "DKA is a medical emergency that should be treated right away.",
    "A dangerous condition that may develop if high levels of ketones are left untreated.",
    "The management of diabetic ketoacidosis in adults" .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/complication/diabetic-kidney-disease> <https://example.org/dmo#definition>
    "Diabetic kidney disease (DKD) is defined primarily as ACR $30 mg/g", "提高医务人员对糖尿病慢性并发症的早期发现、规范化诊断和治疗能力，及早干预治疗糖尿病肾脏病、糖尿病视网膜病变、糖尿病足病等并发症，延缓并发症进展，降低致残率和致死率。",
    "Diabetic kidney disease is a type of kidney disease caused by diabetes.", "Your health care team may check your kidneys at the beginning of your pregnancy. If you already have kidney disease, your team may follow up more closely.",
    "Diabetic kidney disease, also called diabetic nephropathy, is kidney disease caused by diabetes." .

