    "Hypoglycemia is a condition in which blood glucose levels fall below normal, potentially leading to neurological symptoms and requiring urgent intervention.",
    "blood sugar that is too low", "If you take insulin or certain diabetes medicines, drinking alcohol can make your blood glucose level drop too low, which is called hypoglycemia.",
    "Some diabetes medicines can cause hypoglycemia, also called low blood glucose, if you don’t balance your medicines with food and activity.",
    "When your blood glucose level is too low, it is called hypoglycemia.", "Hypoglycemia is a condition in which blood glucose levels fall below normal, leading to symptoms such as confusion, sweating, tremors, and in severe cases, loss of consciousness or seizures." .

