<https://example.org/dmo/id/riskFactor/albuminuria> <https://example.org/dmo#evidenceNote>
    "An ACE inhibitor (ACEi) or angiotensin II receptor blocker (ARB) is recommended for patients with T1D or T2D who have hypertension and albuminuria, titrated to the maximum antihypertensive or highest tolerated dose." .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/riskFactor/age-35-or-older> <https://example.org/dmo#evidenceNote>
    "are age 35 or older. Children and teens can also develop type 2 diabetes, but the risk increases as a person gets older.",
    "Age is a non-modifiable risk factor for type 2 diabetes." .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/riskFactor/family-history-of-type-2-diabetes> <https://example.org/dmo#evidenceNote>
    "文档中明确指出有父母、兄弟或姐妹患有2型糖尿病是风险因素，且无法改变。", "文档中明确指出，如果您有2型糖尿病的家族史，您更有可能患上2型糖尿病。", "have a family history of type 2 diabetes." .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/riskFactor/physical-inactivity-less-than-3-times-a-week>
  <https://example.org/dmo#evidenceNote> "文档中明确指出每周体力活动少于3次是风险因素，并且建议通过增加活动来降低风险。" .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/riskFactor/gestational-diabetes> <https://example.org/dmo#evidenceNote>
    "文档中明确指出曾患有妊娠期糖尿病是风险因素，属于妊娠相关因素。", "妊娠期糖尿病在产后通常会消失，但会增加未来患2型糖尿病的风险。" .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/riskFactor/polycystic-ovary-syndrome> <https://example.org/dmo#evidenceNote>
    "文档中明确指出多囊卵巢综合征是风险因素，属于妊娠相关因素。", "多囊卵巢综合征是糖尿病的重要妇产科相关危险因素。" .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/riskFactor/smoking> <https://example.org/dmo#evidenceNote>
    "Though specific evidence is low, smoking cessation is also strongly advised.", "吸烟是糖尿病的重要危险因素，需通过戒烟干预进行控制。",
    "Smoking raises your risk of developing heart disease. If you have diabetes, it is important to stop smoking, because both smoking and diabetes narrow blood vessels.",
    "文档建议吸烟者应寻求帮助戒烟，暗示吸烟是可干预的风险因素。", "Smoking can lower the amount of blood flow to your feet.",
    "文档明确指出，为了预防糖尿病相关神经损伤，应寻求帮助戒烟。", "The document states that smoking increases the chance of stillbirth or preterm birth and recommends stopping as soon as possible.",
    "Not smoking can help prevent heart disease and stroke, and eye disease.", "smoke External link, including tobacco products and e-cigarettes External link, or are exposed to secondhand smoke External link." .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/riskFactor/prediabetes> <https://example.org/dmo#evidenceNote>
    "Having prediabetes is a risk factor for developing type 2 diabetes.", "文档中明确指出，患有前期糖尿病的人未来患2型糖尿病的风险更高。",
    "糖尿病前期时血糖水平高于正常但未达到糖尿病诊断标准，也可能开始出现视网膜血管损伤。" .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/riskFactor/overweight> <https://example.org/dmo#evidenceNote>
    "超重是糖尿病的重要危险因素，需通过健康生活方式干预进行控制。", "You are also more likely to develop nerve damage if you have diabetes and are overweight.",
    "文档中明确指出，如果患有糖尿病，管理体重可能带来多种健康益处，并建议通过健康饮食、减少卡路里摄入、增加体力活动和保证充足睡眠来达到或维持健康体重。", "People are more likely to develop type 2 diabetes if they have overweight, obesity, or a large waist size." .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/riskFactor/obesity> <https://example.org/dmo#evidenceNote>
    "Obesity is associated with a higher risk of obesity-related complications, along with economic and societal impact.",
    "肥胖是糖尿病的重要危险因素，需通过健康生活方式干预进行控制。", "文档指出，管理糖尿病包括控制体重，以防止神经损伤恶化。", "文档中提到，如果成人超重或肥胖，应与医疗团队合作制定减重计划，并指出减重5%至7%可改善健康问题和血糖、胆固醇、血压水平。",
    "People are more likely to develop type 2 diabetes if they have overweight, obesity, or a large waist size." .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/riskFactor/high-blood-pressure> <https://example.org/dmo#evidenceNote>
    "High blood pressure can cause a heart attack or stroke and damage your kidneys and eyes.",
    "文档提到管理血压是糖尿病ABC管理的一部分，与血糖、胆固醇并列，暗示其为可干预风险因素。", "The document states that high blood pressure can damage kidneys and that controlling it helps protect kidneys, indicating it is modifiable.",
    "文档指出，管理糖尿病包括控制血压，以防止神经损伤恶化。", "Managing your blood pressure can help prevent heart disease and stroke." .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/riskFactor/abnormal-cholesterol-levels> <https://example.org/dmo#evidenceNote>
    "LDL, often called “bad” cholesterol, can build up and clog your blood vessels. High levels of LDL cholesterol raise your risk of developing heart disease. HDL is sometimes called “good cholesterol.” Higher levels of HDL is linked to lower risk for heart disease and stroke. To improve LDL and HDL levels, limit the amount of fat in your eating plan, eat more plant-based foods, and get regular physical activity. Another type of blood fat, triglycerides, also can raise your risk of heart disease when the levels are higher than recommended by your health care team." .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/riskFactor/acute-kidney-injury> <https://example.org/dmo#evidenceNote>
    "Acute kidney injury contributes to reduced metformin clearance, increasing the risk of metformin-associated lactic acidosis.",
    "An 84-year-old woman with T2DM on high dose sulfonylurea therapy admitted with a urinary tract infection and acute kidney injury would be at substantially higher risk of hypoglycaemia." .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/riskFactor/atherosclerotic-cardiovascular-disease> <https://example.org/dmo#evidenceNote>
    "A statin is recommended for all patients with T1D or T2D and CKD, moderate intensity for primary prevention of atherosclerotic cardiovascular disease (ASCVD) or high intensity for patients with known ASCVD and some patients with multiple ASCVD risk factors." .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/riskFactor/hypertension> <https://example.org/dmo#evidenceNote>
    "An ACE inhibitor (ACEi) or angiotensin II receptor blocker (ARB) is recommended for patients with T1D or T2D who have hypertension and albuminuria, titrated to the maximum antihypertensive or highest tolerated dose.",
    "If HTN/CKD, prescribe ACE Inhibitor or ARB unless contraindicated" .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/riskFactor/limited-life-expectancy> <https://example.org/dmo#evidenceNote>
    "Limited life expectancy is a factor that may lead to higher HbA1c targets, as the harms of intensive treatment may outweigh benefits.",
    "Less strict blood glucose control, or an A1C between 7 and 8 percent—or even higher in some circumstances—may be appropriate in people who have limited life expectancy" .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/riskFactor/low-cardiovascular-risk> <https://example.org/dmo#evidenceNote>
    "Low cardiovascular risk is defined as 10-year ASCVD risk <15% and influences the choice of less stringent BP targets." .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/riskFactor/certain-medicines> <https://example.org/dmo#evidenceNote>
    "文档中明确列出某些药物（如利尿剂和皮质类固醇）是 DKA 的其他原因之一。" .

