<https://example.org/dmo/id/contra-SGLT2i-ESRD> <https://example.org/dmo#rationale>
    "Do not take these drugs if you have severe kidney problems or are on dialysis." .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/contra-Bromocriptine-Breastfeeding> <https://example.org/dmo#rationale>
    "Do not take this medicine if you are breastfeeding." .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/contra-TZD-HeartFailure> <https://example.org/dmo#rationale>
    "Before you start taking these drugs, tell your doctor if you have heart failure." .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/contra-SU-RenalHepatic> <https://example.org/dmo#rationale>
    "Older adults and people with kidney or liver problems may be more likely to have low blood sugar when taking these medicines." .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/contra-SGLT2i-RenalHepatic> <https://example.org/dmo#rationale>
    "Before you take these drugs, tell your doctor if you have kidney or liver problems." .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/contra-Biguanide-Renal> <https://example.org/dmo#rationale>
    "People who drink a lot of alcohol and people with kidney problems may have a rare side effect called lactic acidosis (acid to build up in the blood)." .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/contraindication/acarbose-use-not-recommended-with-egfr-30-ml-min-1-73-m2>
  <https://example.org/dmo#rationale> "Use not recommended" .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/contraindication/canagliflozin-initiation-not-recommended-with-egfr-20-ml-min-1-73-m2>
  <https://example.org/dmo#rationale> "Initiation not recommended; may continue 100 mg daily if tolerated for kidney and CV benefit until dialysis" .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/contraindication/consider-dose-reduction-of-metformin-in-the-presence-of-conditions-that-predispose-patients-to-hypoperfusion-and-hypoxemia-for-egfr-45-59-ml-min-1-73-m2>
  <https://example.org/dmo#rationale> "Consider dose reduction in the presence of conditions that predispose patients to hypoperfusion and hypoxemia for eGFR 45 –59 mL/min/1.73 m 2" .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/contraindication/dapagliflozin-initiation-not-recommended-with-egfr-25-ml-min-1-73-m2>
  <https://example.org/dmo#rationale> "Initiation not recommended with eGFR <25 mL/min/1.73 m2; may continue if tolerated for kidney and CV benefit until dialysis" .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/contraindication/empagliflozin-initiation-not-recommended-with-egfr-20-ml-min-1-73-m2>
  <https://example.org/dmo#rationale> "Initiation not recommended with eGFR <20 mL/min/1.73 m2; may continue if tolerated for kidney and CV benefit until dialysis" .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/contraindication/euglycemic-ketoacidosis-with-minimal-to-no-elevation-in-blood-glucose>
  <https://example.org/dmo#rationale> "Euglycemic ketoacidosis with minimal to no elevation in blood glucose may occur in patients taking SGLT2i. Patients with T2D requiring insulin are at particular risk. To mitigate risk, it is important to maintain at least low-dose insulin and consider pausing SGLT2i treatment during periods of acute illness or stressors." .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/contraindication/exenatide-use-not-recommended-with-egfr-30-ml-min-1-73-m2>
  <https://example.org/dmo#rationale> "Use not recommended" .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/contraindication/glyburide-use-not-recommended> <https://example.org/dmo#rationale>
    "Use not recommended" .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/contraindication/hold-sglt2i-during-illness> <https://example.org/dmo#rationale>
    "Hold SGLT2i during illness" .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/contraindication/lixisenatide-use-not-recommended-with-egfr-30-ml-min-1-73-m2>
  <https://example.org/dmo#rationale> "Use not recommended" .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/contraindication/maintain-at-least-low-dose-insulin-in-insulin-requiring-individuals-during-sglt2i-use>
  <https://example.org/dmo#rationale> "Maintain at least low-dose insulin in insulin-requiring individuals" .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/contraindication/metformin-associated-lactic-acidosis>
  <https://example.org/dmo#rationale> "Metformin is excreted unchanged in urine, and impaired metformin excretion in patients with CKD increases the risk of lactic acidosis; most episodes occur concurrent with other acute illness, often when AKI reduces metformin clearance" .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/contraindication/metformin-contraindicated-with-egfr-30-ml-min-1-73-m2>
  <https://example.org/dmo#rationale> "Contraindicated" .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/contraindication/miglitol-use-not-recommended-with-egfr-30-ml-min-1-73-m2>
  <https://example.org/dmo#rationale> "Use not recommended" .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/contraindication/alcohol-use> <https://example.org/dmo#rationale>
    "People who drink a lot of alcohol and people with kidney problems may have a rare side effect called lactic acidosis (acid to build up in the blood)." .

